PLR 3.3: the instance receiver is the FIRST positional parameter,
whatever its name; ~20 converter sites key on the literal name
'self' (instance-attribute registration in __init__, bound-method
calling convention, shadow tracking), so a method using `s` loses
attribute binding entirely. Whole-group fix: a per-method
receiver-name (set at def conversion) replacing the literal
comparisons. Found via the k5 __eq__ dispatch work (its class used
`s`).
